BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Taming of the Shrew
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T215500
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-801@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare's battle-of-the-sexes comedy with an all-female+ c
 ast\, one of three comedies in an August repertory.\n\nHeadstrong Katherin
 e cannot marry off fast enough to suit her father\, and her younger sister
  cannot marry until she does. Enter Petruchio\, a bachelor as loud as Kath
 erine is sharp\, and the sparring begins. Whether the play's "taming" is c
 omedy or cruelty has been argued for centuries\; here an all-female+ cast\
 , directed by Rachel Frawley\, takes it on for the Atlanta Shakespeare Com
 pany. Part of an August repertory alternating three Shakespeare comedies\;
  this production runs through September 3.
GEO:33.768171;-84.3851523
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154233Z
LOCATION:Shakespeare Tavern Playhouse\, 499 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.shakespearetavern.com/on-stage/company/august-threepeat-sh
 rew-comedy-of-errors-and-twelfth-night-in-repertory
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:H.M.S. Pinafore
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260807T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1134@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:Gilbert and Sullivan's 1878 comic opera: a captain's daughter\
 , a common sailor\, and a shipload of class satire.\n\nGilbert and Sulliva
 n's first international hit\, from 1878. Aboard a Royal Navy warship\, the
  captain's daughter Josephine loves Ralph Rackstraw\, a lowly sailor\, whi
 le her father has promised her to Sir Joseph Porter\, a First Lord of the 
 Admiralty who rose to run the Navy without ever going to sea. Cue elopemen
 t plans\, a chorus of sisters\, cousins\, and aunts\, and a late revelatio
 n that turns the whole ship upside down. From the Front Porch Players\, a 
 Clayton County community theatre\; runs through August 16.
GEO:33.5144767;-84.3301925
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154214Z
LOCATION:First Presbyterian Church of Jonesboro\, 1842 Lake Jodeco Rd
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://search.seatyourself.biz/webstore/accounts/thefrontporchplayers
 /buy-tix?landingMessageSeen=true
END:VEVENT
