DESCRIPTION:A book-in-hand reading of John Patrick Shanley's midlife roman
 ce set in a Brooklyn laundromat.\n\nJohn Patrick Shanley — the playwrigh
 t of Doubt and screenwriter of Moonstruck — sets this one in a Brooklyn 
 laundromat\, where the shop's owner and a guarded customer edge toward a m
 idlife romance while illness and family obligation press in at the edges. 
 The play premiered off-Broadway in 2024. Authenticity Theater presents it 
 as a staged reading: actors script in hand\, staging kept minimal\, the wo
 rds doing the work.
