BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Measure for Measure
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T143000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1453@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare's problem play: a disguised duke\, a puritan deput
 y\, and a novice nun bargaining for her brother's life.\n\nThe Duke of Vie
 nna orders his city's dormant morality laws enforced\, hands power to his 
 strict deputy Angelo\, and pretends to leave town. In truth he stays\, dis
 guised as a friar\, to watch what his deputy does with the job. What Angel
 o does is sentence young Claudio to death for fornication\, and when Claud
 io's sister Isabella\, a novice nun\, comes to plead for mercy\, he names 
 a price she cannot pay with a clear conscience. The First Folio filed it w
 ith the comedies\, but its executions and moral bargaining have long earne
 d it the label of problem play. From the Atlanta Shakespeare Company\, per
 formed with tavern table seating and food and drink service.
GEO:33.768171;-84.3851523
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154233Z
LOCATION:Shakespeare Tavern Playhouse\, 499 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.shakespearetavern.com/on-stage/company/measure-for-measure
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Annie
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T143000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1689@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:Strouse and Charnin's 1977 Tony-winning orphan-meets-billionai
 re musical\, opening Aurora Theatre's 31st season.\n\nThe 1977 Tony winner
  for Best Musical\, drawn from Harold Gray's comic strip. In Depression-er
 a New York\, eleven-year-old Annie escapes Miss Hannigan's orphanage\, tak
 es up with a stray dog she names Sandy\, and lands a Christmas invitation 
 to billionaire Oliver Warbucks's mansion\, all while holding out hope that
  her parents will come back for her. Charles Strouse and Martin Charnin's 
 songs include "Tomorrow" and "It's the Hard Knock Life." Bethany Irby Okie
  directs for Aurora Theatre\, with company co-founder Ann-Carol Pence lead
 ing the music. Runs through September 13.
GEO:33.9568797;-83.9880958
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T044316Z
LOCATION:Lawrenceville Arts Center\, 125 N Clayton St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://my.lvilleartscenter.com/146033/146063
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Guys presented by THP Second Stage
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T163000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-2705@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Anne Nelson's two-hander: a fire captain and the editor who he
 lps him write eulogies after 9/11.\n\nAnne Nelson's drama drawn from a tru
 e story: in the weeks after September 11\, 2001\, a New York fire captain 
 has to eulogize the firefighters he lost and can't find the words\, so an 
 editor sits down to help him turn memories into tributes. Just two actors\
 , and more warmth and humor in it than the premise suggests. From the Henr
 y Players' Second Stage series\; runs 75 minutes with one intermission.
GEO:33.4486439;-84.1418279
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154217Z
LOCATION:The Henry Players Theater\, 136 Hood St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/the-guys-presented-by-thp-second-stage-tic
 kets-283661
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Parade
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260913T150000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-936@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:Uhry and Brown's Tony-winning musical of the 1913 Leo Frank ca
 se\, a history that ended in Marietta itself.\n\nAlfred Uhry and Jason Rob
 ert Brown's musical dramatization of the Leo Frank case: a Jewish factory 
 manager from Brooklyn\, convicted in 1913 of murdering thirteen-year-old w
 orker Mary Phagan while an ambitious prosecutor and a sensation-hungry pre
 ss fanned the flames. At the show's center is Frank's marriage\, as his wi
 fe Lucille grows from distant spouse into his fiercest advocate. The origi
 nal won Tony Awards for Uhry's book and Brown's score\, and the 2023 Broad
 way revival won Best Revival of a Musical. The history it dramatizes ended
  with Frank's 1915 lynching in Marietta\, the very town where this perform
 ance is staged.
GEO:33.9536122;-84.5492054
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154236Z
LOCATION:The Strand Theatre\, 117 N Park Square
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://thestrand.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/instances/a0FPs0000
 06VSPZMA4
END:VEVENT
