BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Macbeth
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T214500
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1462@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Shakespeare's Scottish tragedy of witches\, prophecy\, and a c
 ouple who won't wait for fate\, from the Atlanta Shakespeare Company.\n\nT
 hree witches hail a victorious Scottish general as a future king\, and he 
 and his wife decide not to leave the crown to chance. Shakespeare's shorte
 st tragedy traces their climb from prophecy to murder to guilt that will n
 ot wash off. From the Atlanta Shakespeare Company\, performed with food an
 d drink served at your table. A 2025 Suzi Bass Awards Recommended Show.
GEO:33.768171;-84.3851523
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154233Z
LOCATION:Shakespeare Tavern Playhouse\, 499 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.shakespearetavern.com/on-stage/company/macbeth
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ripcord
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T220000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1600@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:David Lindsay-Abaire's comedy of two mismatched retirement-hom
 e roommates and the prank war that spirals between them.\n\nDavid Lindsay-
 Abaire's comedy set in a shared room at the Bristol Place Senior Living Fa
 cility\, where the cantankerous Abby wants her sunny upper-floor quarters 
 to herself and the relentlessly cheerful new arrival Marilyn refuses to bu
 dge. What starts as a bet between the two women spirals into increasingly 
 outrageous pranks\, and each round unearths secrets both would prefer stay
 ed buried. From Stage Door Theatre.
GEO:33.9447222;-84.3319444
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Stage Door Theatre\, 5339 Chamblee Dunwoody Rd
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://ci.ovationtix.com/36385/performance/11823389/selecttickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T220000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1767@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:August Wilson's Pulitzer winner: a former Negro League star in
  1950s Pittsburgh\, at war with his son's dreams.\n\nAugust Wilson's 1985 
 drama\, sixth in his ten-play Pittsburgh Cycle and winner of the Pulitzer 
 Prize and the Tony for Best Play. Troy Maxson was a Negro League baseball 
 star before the color barrier broke\; now he hauls trash\, builds a fence 
 in his yard\, and refuses to let his son chase a college football scholars
 hip\, convinced the game will break the boy the way it broke him. Theatric
 al Outfit produces in partnership with Dominion Entertainment Group and th
 e Alabama Shakespeare Festival\, a two-state revival of the play.
GEO:33.757035;-84.389486
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154239Z
LOCATION:Theatrical Outfit\, 84 Luckie St NW
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brews & Boos: Haunted Pub Crawl
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-4338@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
DESCRIPTION:A grown-up ghost tour with drink stops along the way\, from Au
 rora Theatre's Lawrenceville Ghost Tours crew.\n\nLawrenceville is the old
 est city in metro Atlanta\, and — as the tour's lore has it — the reno
 vation of its historic downtown stirred long-sleeping ghosts awake\, with 
 reports of paranormal activity rising ever since. This is the adult spin o
 n Aurora Theatre's Lawrenceville Ghost Tours: guided ghost stories with pu
 b stops built in\, so you can steady your nerves between hauntings.
GEO:33.9568797;-83.9880958
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T044316Z
LOCATION:Lawrenceville Arts Center\, 125 N Clayton St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://my.lvilleartscenter.com/148304/148309
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:THE PILLOWMAN
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T200000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-8461@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Martin McDonagh's pitch-black thriller: a writer interrogated 
 when child murders start mirroring his grim fairy tales.\n\nMartin McDonag
 h's 2003 play follows Katurian\, a writer of gruesome fairy tales living u
 nder a police state\, hauled in for questioning when a string of child mur
 ders looks suspiciously like his fiction. Two detectives run a good cop/ba
 d cop interrogation while the line between the stories and the crimes keep
 s dissolving. It is McDonagh at his most extreme — very funny and genuin
 ely disturbing\, often in the same beat — and it won the Olivier Award f
 or Best New Play. Produced by Out of Box Theatre.
GEO:33.9148699;-84.3601692
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154224Z
LOCATION:Out of Box Theatre\, 585 Cobb Pkwy SE\, Suite G-1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/the-pillowman-3
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:i never asked for a gofundme
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T200000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-37@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:A world-premiere play: top surgery mistaken for breast cancer\
 , and a small-town GoFundMe nobody asked for.\n\nMillie and her partner Av
 ery are riding out Avery's recovery from gender-affirming top surgery in M
 illie's hometown of Mobile\, Alabama. Then a nosy evangelical family frien
 d misreads the surgery as a breast-cancer fight and launches a GoFundMe on
  the couple's behalf\, making them the talk of the town and the recipients
  of donations they never wanted. Whether to keep the money\, and what keep
 ing it would cost them\, is the question. A world premiere from Actor's Ex
 press.
GEO:33.7817253;-84.4160629
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154154Z
LOCATION:King Plow Arts Center\, 887 W Marietta St NW\, Suite J-107
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://purchase.actors-express.com/EventAvailability?EventId=32801
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Only Light in Reno
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T200000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1439@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Topher Payne's play imagines Marilyn Monroe and Elizabeth Tayl
 or alone together in a blacked-out Reno hotel\, 1960.\n\nAugust 1960: a fo
 rest fire has knocked out the power\, and in a darkened hotel Marilyn Monr
 oe and Elizabeth Taylor find themselves alone in the same room for the onl
 y time in their lives. In Atlanta playwright Topher Payne's telling\, it d
 oes not go well. DeWayne Morgan directs for Onstage Atlanta. Runs through 
 October 4.
GEO:33.7932167;-84.2681503
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154223Z
LOCATION:OnStage Atlanta\, 3041 N Decatur Rd
