BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Buena Vista Social Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1349@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:National touring production of the Broadway musical behind Cub
 a's landmark 1997 album\, sung entirely in Spanish.\n\nThe Broadway musica
 l built from the songs of the 1997 Buena Vista Social Club album: singer O
 mara Portuondo\, once celebrated across Cuba as the "Queen of Feeling\," h
 as long vanished from the spotlight when a young record producer arrives w
 ith one more chance at the studio. The story moves between 1990s Havana an
 d the musicians' younger selves in the 1950s\, and the score — son\, dan
 zón\, bolero — is performed entirely in Spanish. Book by Marco Ramirez\
 , with choreography by Justin Peck and Patricia Delgado\; the show won a S
 pecial Tony Award for its live onstage musicians and a Grammy for its cast
  album. A national touring production.
GEO:33.7726136;-84.3853395
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154214Z
LOCATION:Fox Theatre\, 660 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://foxtheatre.evenue.net/cgi-bin/ncommerce3/SEGetGroupList?groupC
 ode=BVS&linkID=fta&shopperContext=&caller=&appCode=
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jeffrey Hatcher's The Turn of the Screw
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261028T210000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1476@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Two actors\, one piano\, and Henry James's ghost story perform
 ed in the round — no intermission\, one week only.\n\nJeffrey Hatcher's 
 adaptation of Henry James's 1898 novella: a new governess arrives at an En
 glish manor and begins seeing ghosts around the children in her care\, inc
 luding the specter of the woman who held the job before her. Whether the h
 auntings are real or her own fevered invention is the question the play ke
 eps turning. Two actors carry the whole story\, performed in the round wit
 h live atmospheric piano. From the Atlanta Shakespeare Company\; a one-wee
 k run with no intermission and no latecomer seating.
GEO:33.768171;-84.3851523
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Shakespeare Tavern Playhouse\, 499 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.shakespearetavern.com/on-stage/company/jeffrey-hatchers-th
 e-turn-of-the-screw
END:VEVENT
