BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brews & Boos: Haunted Pub Crawl
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-4346@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
DESCRIPTION:A grown-up ghost tour with drink stops along the way\, from Au
 rora Theatre's Lawrenceville Ghost Tours crew.\n\nLawrenceville is the old
 est city in metro Atlanta\, and — as the tour's lore has it — the reno
 vation of its historic downtown stirred long-sleeping ghosts awake\, with 
 reports of paranormal activity rising ever since. This is the adult spin o
 n Aurora Theatre's Lawrenceville Ghost Tours: guided ghost stories with pu
 b stops built in\, so you can steady your nerves between hauntings.
GEO:33.9568797;-83.9880958
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T044316Z
LOCATION:Lawrenceville Arts Center\, 125 N Clayton St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://my.lvilleartscenter.com/148304/148317
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Other Paths To God
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T200000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-582@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Five ICU nurses\, $3 million missing\, one scandal: a world-pr
 emiere comedy from Atlanta playwright Kelundra Smith.\n\nA world premiere 
 from Atlanta playwright Kelundra Smith\, writer of The Wash. When $3 milli
 on goes missing at Morey Medical Center and fingers point at the ICU's fiv
 e nurses\, everybody's worst behavior comes out. Smith drew on interviews 
 with real Atlanta nurses to write about what it means to give your life to
  a job that doesn't love you back. Commissioned through Horizon Theatre's 
 Black Women Speak program\; runs through November 8.
GEO:33.7620155;-84.3525137
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154217Z
LOCATION:Horizon Theatre\, 1083 Austin Ave NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://tickets.horizontheatre.com/144305/145622
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Superior Donuts
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T200000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1317@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Tracy Letts's comedy-drama of a burned-out donut shop owner an
 d the young writer who shakes him awake.\n\nTracy Letts\, the Pulitzer win
 ner behind August: Osage County\, in a gentler mode: a former '60s radical
  presides over his fading donut shop in Chicago's Uptown until Franco\, a 
 bright young Black writer\, turns up looking for work and full of plans to
  fix the place. Reviewing the 2008 Steppenwolf premiere\, the New York Tim
 es's Charles Isherwood called it "insubstantial and sweet" yet "hard to di
 slike." Robby Myles directs for Authenticity Theater. Runs through October
  31.
GEO:33.7639125;-84.3509364
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154201Z
LOCATION:7 Stages Theatre\, 1105 Euclid Ave NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://authenticitytheater.ludus.com/index.php?sections=events
END:VEVENT
