SUMMARY:Like Father
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T220000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-183@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musical Theatre
DESCRIPTION:New folk-pop musical: after her father's arrest\, a teenager's
  family becomes true-crime podcast fodder.\n\nA world-premiere coming-of-a
 ge musical written by Jacob Ryan Smith and Caroline Pernick\, from Allianc
 e Theatre. Seventeen-year-old Chris\, reeling from her father's arrest\, l
 ands with the estranged mother and stepfather she barely knows\, until a h
 it true-crime podcast drags the family's buried past into public view. The
  folk-pop score draws on the stories of relatives left behind by infamous 
 killers\, and on an industry that has grown to 250 million listeners. Tina
 she Kajese-Bolden directs\; the show won the first Open Jar Broadway Shark
  Tank and runs through November 15.
GEO:33.7893845;-84.3846553
LAST-MODIFIED:20260726T205057Z
LOCATION:Woodruff Arts Center\, 1280 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://my.alliancetheatre.org/164244/164508
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It's a Wonderful Life: A Live Radio Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-943@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Capra's 1946 Christmas classic restaged as a live 1940s radio 
 broadcast\, with onstage foley effects and actors doubling dozens of roles
 .\n\nThe story of George Bailey\, the Bedford Falls building-and-loan man 
 who hits bottom one snowy Christmas Eve and gets shown what his town would
  look like if he'd never been born. This adaptation of Frank Capra's 1946 
 film plays out as a period radio broadcast: a small ensemble at vintage mi
 crophones voicing dozens of characters\, with every footstep\, door slam\,
  and ringing bell made live by a foley artist in full view. Presented by T
 he Strand Theatre.
GEO:33.9536122;-84.5492054
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154236Z
LOCATION:The Strand Theatre\, 117 N Park Square
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://thestrand.my.salesforce-sites.com/ticket/#/instances/a0FPs0000
 06WQrxMAG
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vanya and Sonia and Masha and Spike
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261106T213000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1266@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Christopher Durang's Chekhov-riffing comedy: a movie-star sist
 er\, her young boyfriend\, and a family farmhouse up for sale.\n\nChristop
 her Durang's comedy borrows its names and its moods from Chekhov\, then le
 ts them loose in present-day Pennsylvania. Siblings Vanya and Sonia have s
 pent their quiet lives in the family farmhouse\; their movie-star sister M
 asha blows in for the weekend with her much younger boyfriend Spike and an
 nounces she's selling the place. Rivalry\, regret\, and a costume party fo
 llow. The play won the 2013 Tony Award for Best Play\; this production com
 es from Arcadia Theater.
GEO:34.0765277;-84.2884766
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154157Z
LOCATION:Arcadia Theater\, 180 Academy St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
