BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All is Calm: The Christmas Truce of 1914
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261213T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261213T160000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-383@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
DESCRIPTION:Peter Rothstein's a cappella retelling of the WWI Christmas tr
 uce\, built from soldiers' letters and period songs.\n\nOn Christmas Eve 1
 914\, soldiers along the Western Front laid down their rifles\, crossed no
 -man's land\, and sang together. Peter Rothstein's documentary-style music
 al tells that true story through trench songs\, patriotic tunes\, and caro
 ls\, sung a cappella and woven with the soldiers' own words from letters a
 nd journals. Music by Erick Lichte and Timothy C. Takach. Presented by The
  Atlanta Opera as part of its Discoveries series.
GEO:33.757035;-84.389486
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154158Z
LOCATION:Theatrical Outfit\, 84 Luckie St NW
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.theatricaloutfit.org/whats-on/all-is-calm-the-christmas-tr
 uce-of-1914/book/64402
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Dickens Christmas
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261213T143000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-449@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:A farce about a theatre troupe's disastrous attempt to stage A
  Christmas Carol\, back for a second year.\n\nNot A Christmas Carol itself
 \, but a comedy about trying to perform it: an earnest theatre troupe take
 s on the Dickens classic and everything that can go wrong does\, from blow
 n cues to full-scale onstage disasters. The holiday warmth survives the wr
 eckage\, more or less. From Cherokee Theatre\, returning for a second year
 \, and suitable for all ages.
GEO:34.2365417;-84.4902423
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154204Z
LOCATION:Canton Theatre\, 171 E Main St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.tix.com/ticket-sales/cherokeetheatre/1960/event/1465856
END:VEVENT
