BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Christmas Carol
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T211500
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-225@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Play
DESCRIPTION:Dickens's Scrooge-and-three-ghosts classic in David H. Bell's 
 adaptation with live music\, from the Alliance Theatre.\n\nCharles Dickens
 's 1843 tale of Ebenezer Scrooge\, the miser visited by the ghosts of Chri
 stmas Past\, Present\, and Yet to Come on a single night of reckoning. The
  Alliance Theatre's annual production uses David H. Bell's adaptation\, st
 aged with live music and a large company of characters. Amanda Watkins dir
 ects\, building on Leora Morris's original staging. Runs through December 
 27.
GEO:33.7893845;-84.3846553
LAST-MODIFIED:20260726T205057Z
LOCATION:Woodruff Arts Center\, 1280 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://my.alliancetheatre.org/164230/164947
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:All is Calm: The Christmas Truce of 1914
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T210000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-387@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
DESCRIPTION:Peter Rothstein's a cappella retelling of the WWI Christmas tr
 uce\, built from soldiers' letters and period songs.\n\nOn Christmas Eve 1
 914\, soldiers along the Western Front laid down their rifles\, crossed no
 -man's land\, and sang together. Peter Rothstein's documentary-style music
 al tells that true story through trench songs\, patriotic tunes\, and caro
 ls\, sung a cappella and woven with the soldiers' own words from letters a
 nd journals. Music by Erick Lichte and Timothy C. Takach. Presented by The
  Atlanta Opera as part of its Discoveries series.
GEO:33.757035;-84.389486
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154158Z
LOCATION:Theatrical Outfit\, 84 Luckie St NW
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.theatricaloutfit.org/whats-on/all-is-calm-the-christmas-tr
 uce-of-1914/book/64203
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It's a Wonderful Life: A Live Radio Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1161@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Joe Landry's radio-play staging of the 1946 Capra classic\, co
 mplete with live foley sound effects and music.\n\nJoe Landry's adaptation
  reframes the 1946 Frank Capra film as a 1940s radio broadcast: a small en
 semble of actors plays every citizen of Bedford Falls\, with sound effects
  and music made live on stage. The story is the one you know from the movi
 e\, where George Bailey hits bottom on Christmas Eve and an angel shows hi
 m what the town would look like if he had never been born. From Merely Pla
 yers\, and family-friendly.
GEO:33.9031178;-84.2776526
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154219Z
LOCATION:Merely Players Presents\, 3785 King Ave
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.merelyplayerspresents.com/event-details/its-a-wonderful-li
 fe-a-live-radio-play-2026-12-19-19-30
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Christmas Story: The Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T213000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1276@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:Ralphie's quest for a Red Ryder BB gun\, sung: the Pasek and P
 aul musical of the 1983 holiday film.\n\nThe 1983 movie that runs on a loo
 p every December\, turned Broadway musical with songs by Benj Pasek and Ju
 stin Paul (later of Dear Evan Hansen) and a book by Joseph Robinette. Nine
 -year-old Ralphie Parker schemes toward the one gift every adult swears wi
 ll shoot his eye out: an Official Red Ryder carbine-action BB gun. The leg
  lamp\, the tongue on the flagpole\, and the pink bunny suit all make it o
 nstage\, in a score The New York Times called "likable" and "perky." From 
 Arcadia Theater.
GEO:34.0765277;-84.2884766
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154157Z
LOCATION:Arcadia Theater\, 180 Academy St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/christmas-story-the-musical-tickets-279858
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mrs. Doubtfire
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1369@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:The 1993 Robin Williams film as a Broadway musical: divorced d
 ad\, Scottish nanny disguise\, national touring production.\n\nThe musical
  adaptation of the 1993 film: Daniel Hillard\, an out-of-work actor who lo
 ses custody of his kids in a messy divorce\, invents Euphegenia Doubtfire\
 , a kindly Scottish nanny\, to stay in their lives. Songs come from Wayne 
 and Karey Kirkpatrick\, the songwriting team behind Something Rotten!\, wi
 th Karey Kirkpatrick and John O'Farrell sharing book duties. Four-time Ton
 y winner Jerry Zaks directs. A national touring production\, presented as 
 part of the Broadway in Atlanta series.
GEO:33.7726136;-84.3853395
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154214Z
LOCATION:Fox Theatre\, 660 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://foxtheatre.evenue.net/cgi-bin/ncommerce3/SEGetGroupList?groupC
 ode=MRS&linkID=fta&shopperContext=&caller=&appCode=
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Charles Dickens' A Christmas Carol
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T213500
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1503@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Dickens' ghost story told by a handful of actors\, with song\,
  an Atlanta Shakespeare Company holiday tradition of 20-plus years.\n\nJ. 
 Tony Brown's adaptation of Dickens' 1843 novella\, a fixture of the Atlant
 a Shakespeare Company's December calendar for more than two decades\, this
  year in a staging by Kati Grace Kirby. The approach is storytelling rathe
 r than spectacle: a small group of performers\, with a bit of song\, follo
 ws the miser Ebenezer Scrooge from his counting house through a Christmas 
 Eve visited by three ghosts and a certain small boy named Tiny Tim. The pl
 ayhouse's dinner-table seating means food and drink arrive during the perf
 ormance.
GEO:33.768171;-84.3851523
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Shakespeare Tavern Playhouse\, 499 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.shakespearetavern.com/on-stage/company/charles-dickens-a-c
 hristmas-carol
END:VEVENT
