BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:12 Angry Jurors
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270207T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270207T170000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-843@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Reginald Rose's jury-room drama: eleven guilty votes\, one hol
 dout\, and a murder verdict hinging on reasonable doubt.\n\nReginald Rose'
 s classic deliberation drama\, here in the retitled version that opens the
  jury room to a cast of any gender. A teenager stands accused of murdering
  his father\, and the first vote comes back eleven to one for guilty. The 
 lone holdout wants to talk it through\, and one hot afternoon in one room\
 , the case starts to come apart. From Southside Theatre Guild\, an all-vol
 unteer community theatre running since 1973.
GEO:33.5672762;-84.5821546
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Southside Theatre Guild\, 20 W Campbellton St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://tockify.com/stgevents/detail/1026/1802048400000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweat
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270207T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270207T163000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1392@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Lynn Nottage's Pulitzer-winning drama of factory friends in a 
 Rust Belt bar as the layoffs begin.\n\nLynn Nottage's 2015 drama\, winner 
 of the 2017 Pulitzer Prize\, set mostly in a bar in Reading\, Pennsylvania
 \, where a circle of steel-plant workers has gathered for years. When one 
 of the friends is promoted to management and jobs start moving to Mexico\,
  the lines between labor and boss\, and along race\, begin to cut through 
 the group. Nottage built the play from years of interviews with residents 
 of Reading\, then one of the poorest cities in America. From the Henry Pla
 yers.
GEO:33.4486439;-84.1418279
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154217Z
LOCATION:The Henry Players Theater\, 136 Hood St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/sweat-tickets-271676
END:VEVENT
