UID:occ-723@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Alcott's four March sisters grow up\, in Thomas Hischak's stag
 e adaptation from Players Guild at Sugar Hill.\n\nLouisa May Alcott's nove
 l of the four March sisters — headstrong Jo\, practical Meg\, gentle Bet
 h\, and ambitious Amy — coming of age in Civil War-era New England\, eac
 h chasing a different idea of what her life should be. Thomas Hischak's st
 age adaptation\, from Players Guild at Sugar Hill.
GEO:34.1070667;-84.0353528
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154225Z
LOCATION:The Eagle Theater\, 5029 W Broad St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://ci.ovationtix.com/36627/performance/11797899/selecttickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Water For Elephants
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270207T183000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1735@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:Sara Gruen's Depression-era circus novel as a musical\, on nat
 ional tour after premiering in Atlanta before Broadway.\n\nDuring the Depr
 ession\, a young man who has just lost everything hops a moving train and 
 lands among the Benzini Brothers circus\, where his veterinary training\, 
 an untrainable elephant named Rosie\, and the ringmaster's wife reshape hi
 s life\, all remembered through the eyes of his older self. Rick Elice ada
 pted the book from Sara Gruen's 2006 novel\, with a score by PigPen Theatr
 e Co. and Rosie brought to life through puppetry. The show premiered in At
 lanta at the Alliance Theatre in 2023 before a Broadway run that earned se
 ven Tony nominations\, including Best Musical. This is the national tourin
 g production.
GEO:33.7726136;-84.3853395
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154214Z
LOCATION:Fox Theatre\, 660 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://foxtheatre.evenue.net/cgi-bin/ncommerce3/SEGetGroupList?groupC
 ode=WAT&linkID=fta&shopperContext=&caller=&appCode=
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Miseducated
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270207T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270207T214500
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-244@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Play
DESCRIPTION:New play from Brandon P. Fleming's memoir: Atlanta debate stud
 ents\, and a coach arguing with the universe itself.\n\nRudi Goblen adapts
  Brandon P. Fleming's memoir into a world premiere commissioned by the All
 iance Theatre. Atlanta high schoolers train for an elite Harvard debate pr
 ogram under a coach who demands they sharpen every argument. Then Brandon 
 gets pulled into a surreal debate of his own\, arguing with the universe o
 ver the memories that made him and whether a life can be rewritten. Teo Ca
 stellanos directs\, with the story told through debate rounds\, music\, an
 d spoken word. Runs through February 21.
GEO:33.7893845;-84.3846553
LAST-MODIFIED:20260726T205057Z
LOCATION:Woodruff Arts Center\, 1280 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://my.alliancetheatre.org/164246/164535
END:VEVENT
