BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lauren Gunderson's The Book of Will
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270403T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1543@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Theatre
DESCRIPTION:Gunderson's true story of the two actors who saved half of Sha
 kespeare's plays by printing the First Folio.\n\nAfter Shakespeare's death
 \, his fellow actors Henry Condell and John Heminges set out to collect an
 d publish his plays as the First Folio\, without which roughly half of the
 m would have vanished. Lauren Gunderson\, the Atlanta-born writer who has 
 repeatedly topped American Theatre's list of the country's most-produced l
 iving playwrights\, spins the history into a story of friendship\, grief\,
  and stubborn devotion to the words. From the Atlanta Shakespeare Company\
 , performed with the tavern's table seating and food and drink service.
GEO:33.768171;-84.3851523
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Shakespeare Tavern Playhouse\, 499 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.shakespearetavern.com/on-stage/company/lauren-gundersons-t
 he-book-of-will
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Shop of Horrors
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270403T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270403T223000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1634@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:Menken and Ashman's doo-wop horror comedy: a skid row florist\
 , a bloodthirsty plant\, and a Faustian bargain.\n\nThe 1982 horror-comedy
  musical from Alan Menken and Howard Ashman\, the songwriting team that la
 ter gave Disney The Little Mermaid. Meek flower-shop clerk Seymour discove
 rs a strange plant that turns his fortunes around\, but Audrey II has a ta
 ste for blood and an appetite that keeps growing. The score runs on early-
 '60s rock and roll\, doo-wop\, and Motown\, with a girl-group trio of stre
 et urchins as Greek chorus. Presented by Stage Door Theatre.
GEO:33.9447222;-84.3319444
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Stage Door Theatre\, 5339 Chamblee Dunwoody Rd
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://ci.ovationtix.com/36385/performance/11825819/selecttickets
END:VEVENT
