BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Arcadia
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270514T200000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1216@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:2
DESCRIPTION:Tom Stoppard's 1993 comedy of chaos theory\, Byron gossip\, an
 d one country house across two centuries.\n\nTom Stoppard's 1993 play unfo
 lds in a single English country-house room across two centuries. In 1809\,
  teenage math prodigy Thomasina Coverly scribbles ideas decades ahead of h
 er time while her tutor dodges a duel over another man's wife. In the pres
 ent day\, two rival academics comb the same house for evidence of a scanda
 l involving Lord Byron\, and keep getting the past wrong. One 1993 critic 
 grumbled it was 'too clever by about two-and-three-quarters'\; many others
  rank it as Stoppard's finest play. From Pumphouse Players.
GEO:34.1644344;-84.7971239
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154229Z
LOCATION:Pumphouse Players\, 114 W Main St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/arcadia-tickets-1989768662633
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sidekicks Time Machine - An Improvised Musical
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270515
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270516
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1597@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Comedy
DESCRIPTION:A fully improvised musical from Southside Sidekicks — songs\
 , scenes\, and story invented on the spot.\n\nA musical made up in front o
 f you: the Southside Sidekicks\, Southside Theatre Guild's in-house improv
  troupe\, take audience suggestions and spin them into songs\, characters\
 , and a story that has never existed before and never will again. The time
 -machine premise gives the improvisers license to land anywhere in history
  the audience points them.
GEO:33.5672762;-84.5821546
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Southside Theatre Guild\, 20 W Campbellton St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
