BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Hunchback of Notre Dame
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270611T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270611T213000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1405@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:Disney's stage musical of Hugo's bell-ringer tale\, with the M
 enken and Schwartz score\, from the Henry Players.\n\nThe stage musical dr
 awn from Disney's 1996 animated film\, itself adapted from Victor Hugo's 1
 831 Gothic novel. Quasimodo\, the bell-ringer hidden away in Notre Dame's 
 tower\, longs for the world beyond the cathedral walls and finds a friend 
 in Esmeralda\, a Romani woman who stands up to his cruel guardian\, Judge 
 Frollo. The Alan Menken and Stephen Schwartz score is darker and more seri
 ous than most of the Disney songbook. A volunteer community production fro
 m the Henry Players.
GEO:33.4486439;-84.1418279
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154217Z
LOCATION:The Henry Players Theater\, 136 Hood St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.simpletix.com/e/the-hunchback-of-notre-dame-tickets-269295
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beetlejuice
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270611T193000
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1750@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Musicals
DESCRIPTION:The musical of Tim Burton's 1988 film: a grieving teen\, two h
 apless ghosts\, and a demon summoned by name.\n\nThe Broadway musical base
 d on Tim Burton's 1988 film\, with songs by Eddie Perfect and a book by Sc
 ott Brown and Anthony King. Lydia Deetz\, a teenager mourning her mother a
 nd ignored by her father\, moves into a house haunted by a recently deceas
 ed couple and a striped-suit demon who turns visible only if the living sa
 y his name three times. New York magazine's critic called it 'loud\, cheek
 y\, and all about excess\,' true to its source. Expect 'Day-O' at the dinn
 er party.
GEO:33.7726136;-84.3853395
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154214Z
LOCATION:Fox Theatre\, 660 Peachtree St NE
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://foxtheatre.evenue.net/cgi-bin/ncommerce3/SEGetGroupList?groupC
 ode=BEE&linkID=fta&shopperContext=&caller=&appCode=
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stand Up for Improv - Improvised Stand-Up Show
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270612
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270613
DTSTAMP:20260729T154349Z
UID:occ-1598@atlcal.com
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Comedy
DESCRIPTION:Stand-up with no prepared material: comics improvise their set
 s live from audience suggestions.\n\nA mash-up of two comedy forms: the pe
 rformers take the stand-up mic\, but every joke is invented on the spot\, 
 built from whatever the audience throws at them. No script\, no tested mat
 erial\, no safety net. Presented by Southside Theatre Guild\, an all-volun
 teer community theatre running since 1973.
GEO:33.5672762;-84.5821546
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T154234Z
LOCATION:Southside Theatre Guild\, 20 W Campbellton St
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://tockify.com/stgevents/detail/1065/1812772800000
END:VEVENT
